{"reference":"Ezekiel 2","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Commission Marked by Resistance","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents Ezekiel’s commission as a demanding encounter: the Spirit sets him on his feet, he is sent to a rebellious people, and he is told to speak whether they listen or refuse. The scroll extended to him, filled with lamentation, mourning, and woe, belongs to this larger picture of a message he must receive and carry. The linked themes continue into the next chapter, where the commission develops further.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 2:1-10"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_002_51fc10a8ffdb2c0de75d6b4e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}